       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision (2,400 mg/day is more typical). The 1,600 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day), common for pain or fever\n- **1,600 mg total daily dose**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll reconsider. I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
